                 msen = 0: RETURN
 9F7C   0C58            '----- ...and bail if the vector points to a bare IRET 
                stub (first byte
 9F7C   0C58            '      &HCF).  That is what is there with NO real drive
                r (e.g. after
 9F7C   0C58            '      exiting Win98 to MS-DOS mode); calling INT 33h o
                n it hangs.  A real
 9F7C   0C58            '      driver's handler starts with executable code (mo
                use.com begins with
 9F7C   0C58            '      a JMP, &HEB), never a bare IRET (&HCF) or a 0/de
                ad byte -- so this
 9F7C   0C58            '      tells a real driver from a dead leftover vector 
